   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ec3abf0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Stage 4: Leakage-Safe Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "Stage 4 builds a moderate, interpretable feature set and uses a fixed Ridge regression only as a lightweight information check. It is not the Stage 5 model comparison. No tree model, boosting model, Kaggle test prediction, or submission is created.\n",
    "\n",
    "The shared training and validation feature matrices are built **once**. All four experiments reuse them and select different column subsets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "6614d438",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-15T14:45:50.588057Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-15T14:45:50.587905Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-15T14:45:57.513561Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-15T14:45:57.513165Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Shared training matrix: 648,648 rows\n",
      "Validation: 2017-07-31 to 2017-08-15 (28,512 rows)\n",
      "Raw engineered columns: 28; best encoded columns: 29\n",
      "Leakage perturbation check passed: True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import matplotlib\n",
    "matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def find_root(start=Path.cwd()):\n",
    "    for candidate in (start, *start.parents):\n",
    "        if (candidate / \"src\" / \"features.py\").exists() and (candidate / \"data\" / \"raw\").exists():\n",
    "            return candidate\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Could not locate repository root\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = find_root()\n",
    "if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n",
    "from src.features import (\n",
    "    ALL_FEATURES, BENCHMARK, TARGET_DERIVED, TARGET_LOG,\n",
    "    leakage_perturbation_check, load_raw_data, run_pipeline,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "FIGURE_DIR = ROOT / \"reports\" / \"figures\" / \"features\"\n",
    "REPORT_PATH = ROOT / \"reports\" / \"feature_engineering.md\"\n",
    "FIGURE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "plt.style.use(\"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\")\n",
    "\n",
    "raw = load_raw_data()\n",
    "history, validation, train_features, validation_features, feature_summary, scores, predictions = run_pipeline(raw)\n",
    "leakage_passed = leakage_perturbation_check(raw, validation_features)\n",
    "best = scores.iloc[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Shared training matrix: {len(train_features):,} rows\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation: {validation['date'].min().date()} to {validation['date'].max().date()} ({len(validation):,} rows)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Raw engineered columns: {len(ALL_FEATURES)}; best encoded columns: {int(best['encoded_feature_count'])}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Leakage perturbation check passed: {leakage_passed}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80808f5f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Validation design and leakage risks\n",
    "\n",
    "The split is unchanged from Stage 3: history ends on 30 July 2017 and validation covers 31 July through 15 August (16 days and 28,512 rows). Validation lags use only historical dates; if an ordinary lag would point inside validation, the lookup steps back by whole weeks until it is pre-validation. Rolling summaries are fixed from pre-validation history and repeated across the direct horizon.\n",
    "\n",
    "Changing every validation target to an artificial value leaves all target-derived validation features unchanged. No centered windows, full-data target means, target encoding, or validation-target updates are used."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32b8d52a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Feature groups and missing values\n",
    "\n",
    "- Calendar: weekday, day, month, year, weekend, month boundaries, and payday.\n",
    "- Promotion: raw count, binary indicator, and `log1p` count.\n",
    "- Target-derived: lags 7/14/28, fixed rolling mean 7/28, rolling standard deviation 28, and their transparent `log1p` versions.\n",
    "- Store: type and cluster.\n",
    "- Simplified date context: national non-transferred holiday, transfer day, and filled oil price.\n",
    "\n",
    "Holiday rows are aggregated to one row per date. Local/regional matching is deferred. Oil is filled only in time order within its own series.\n",
    "\n",
    "![Feature columns by group](../reports/figures/features/02_feature_groups.png)"
   ]
  },
